{"Team Builder", "Team Builder", "Team Builder", ""},
{"Team Builder", "Team Builder", "Army", "A faction's army, the Enemy Team below (Custom), or a new random army each match."},
{"Team Builder", "Team Builder", "Team", "The Enemy Team, or one of your saved teams, so each computer can have its own custom army."},
{"Team Builder", "Team Builder", "Colour", "If the colour is taken, or Automatic, it gets the first free one."},
{"Team Builder", "Team Builder", "Allied with the other computers", "On: the computers team up against you. Off: free-for-all."},
{"Team Builder", "Team Builder", "Computers attack each other's bases", "Normally each computer sends its army only at you and fights the other computer only when they meet. On, each computer targets the nearest enemy base, the other computer's included. Not while the computers are allied. Free Play only."},
{"Team Builder", "Team Builder", "Neutral Creatures in Armies", "Adds the Wolf, Robot and Monkey (Close Combat) and the Shark (Special Two) to armies. Costs: Wolf 200 (build 420), Robot 80 (270), Shark 400 (660). The Shark is built at a Shipyard. Online, the host's setting applies."},
{"Team Builder", "Team Builder", "Teal team colour", "Adds Teal as a seventh team colour. Online, the host's setting applies."},
{"Team Builder", "Team Builder", "Team-Colour Unit Portraits", "The small round portraits of the selected units on the top screen take their owner's team colour, like the units do. Off: the game's own red and blue. Only you see it."},
{"Team Builder", "Team Builder", "Proper Creature Portraits", "The Wolf and the Shark show their own heads on the top screen when selected. The game's battle art has a lantern and a sack in their place. Only you see it."},
{"Team Builder", "Team Builder", "Tint creatures by team", "Owned creatures show their owner's team colour. Wild ones don't. Needs the option above. Only you see it."},
{"Team Builder", "Team Builder", "Randomize", "Pick a team from the list to load it. Randomize picks each slot from the units your save has. \"Recent save team\" entries are your save's last five armies, kept automatically in case one gets replaced. They can't be deleted."},
